From 3e67621c819b248f2a907915f4cf92d10b94aecc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cory Forsythe <cory@coryforsythe.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 22:10:45 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 10/24] feat(hermes-vps): fleet-dispatch wiring for the
 VPS-bridged Hermes transport

Adds harness=hermes-vps: a new local bridge process (bin/fm-hermes-vps-bridge.py/.sh)
that gives a captain's remote VPS Hermes /api/ws session an ordinary firstmate pane,
wired into fm-spawn.sh (launch/readiness/delivery, session_id recorded in meta),
fm-busy-lib.sh (live session.status pull), and fm-control-lib.sh/fm-control.sh
(real session.interrupt/session.close, unlike the pane-based hermes adapter).
Live-verified end to end against the real VPS: spawn, busy detection, interrupt,
and exit all round-tripped with no leaked server-side sessions. Two real bugs
found only via live traffic (same-segment event starvation, and the gateway
dropping the connection after a successful interrupt) are fixed with an
event-drain loop and transparent reconnect.
